---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy">
  <section class="hero" style="padding-top: 80px; padding-bottom: 32px;">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: November 13, 2026 · How we collect, use, and protect your information.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>AI Agents Hub is a static-only site</strong> (deployed on GitHub Pages). It runs no
          backend, offers no user accounts, and maintains no database of reader profiles. We do not
          ask you for a name, email address, phone number, government ID, or any other personal
          information in order to browse the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do load third-party measurement and advertising services (described in section 2),
          which process technical identifiers such as your IP address, browser and cookie IDs. The
          technical logs generated directly by the site's hosting are limited to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Request time, requested URL, HTTP status, User-Agent, and Referer — generated by
            <strong>GitHub Pages / CDN edge nodes</strong> for security and operational purposes.</li>
          <li>Anti-bot and cache logs from <strong>Cloudflare</strong> for site
            acceleration and basic protection.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Analytics, advertising and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          This site loads <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> and <strong>Google AdSense</strong>.
          Analytics tells us which pages are read in aggregate; AdSense displays ads. These Google
          services may set cookies or read device identifiers to do so. We do not use this data to
          build individual profiles, and we do not sell it. You can limit it with your browser's
          tracking protection or a content-blocking extension.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside aggregate page views, this site records a small set of
          <strong>anonymous interaction events</strong>: clicks on an agent's official
          website or GitHub repository, clicks on image source links, expanded FAQ
          entries, scroll depth, and whether the on-site search box was used. These
          events contain only the page path, the page type and (for outbound links) the
          destination host — <strong>never</strong> search terms, URL query strings, your
          name, email address, IP address, or any identifier that could be tied to you as
          an individual. Search box usage is counted without recording what was typed.
          We use these events only in aggregate, and we do not build reader profiles from
          them.
        </p>
        <p>
          The only thing this site itself writes to your browser's <code>localStorage</code> is your
          <strong>theme preference</strong> (light / dark / system), used solely to restore your display
          choice on the next visit. This data <strong>stays on your device</strong> and is never uploaded
          to any server.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Third-party services and links</h2>
        <p>
          In addition to Google Analytics 4, Google AdSense and Cloudflare named above, this site
          contains many links to third-party websites (agent homepages, GitHub repositories,
          sign-up pages, etc.). Once you click through and leave this site, <strong>we have no control
          over what those third parties collect</strong> or what cookies they set. Please review each
          third party's privacy policy before visiting.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Embedded resources</h2>
        <p>
          To improve the experience, some agent detail pages may embed videos or posts from
          <strong>YouTube, Bilibili, Loom or X (Twitter)</strong>. These embeds are loaded by their
          respective platforms and may set cookies or collect IP addresses under their own privacy
          policies. If you do not wish to be tracked by these platforms, enable "Block third-party
          cookies" in your browser or use a privacy extension such as uBlock Origin.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          We hold no user accounts and no database of reader profiles. If you contact us by email or
          open a GitHub issue, the personal data involved is limited to what you choose to send. You
          can request access, correction, or deletion of that correspondence at any time via the
          <a href={`${base}/contact`}>contact page</a>; replying "please delete my email" to an
          existing thread is enough. Analytics data is aggregate and cannot be tied back to you by us.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Minors</h2>
        <p>
          This site is aimed at developers and researchers with full civil capacity and is not designed
          for children under 14. If a minor visits the site through a guardian, the same policy
          applies.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Policy updates</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be revised as the site evolves (for example, if a new third-party service
          is added). After a revision, the "Last updated" timestamp at the top of this page will be
          updated; no separate notice will be issued. Continued use of the site indicates acceptance
          of the current version.
        </p>

        <div class="verdict-box" style="margin-top: 32px;">
          <div class="label">TL;DR</div>
          <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--text);">
            Static-only site · no accounts · no reader profiles · aggregate analytics and ads via
            Google · only your theme preference in local storage · corrections welcome via GitHub issues.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
